<@UPBR7JZ3R>, it should not be an issue, as long as we are all on the same page that this is now supposed to work that way, and it is not exactly the same restriction that applied before.

Note that there are three related suspension reasons:
• `car_application_added` — this is the "New car application" suspension that the system automatically adds when a driver creates a new driver application;
• `car_application_added_manual` — this is the "New car application (manual)" suspension that ops can apply themselves to driver;
• `possible_new_car_application` — this is "Possible new car application" suspension that the system applies when driver uploads `v_logbook_else_keeper`, `mot_document`, `uk_vehicle_insurance`, `uk_private_hire_vehicle_licence` documents.
Please confirm if *only* `car_application_added` should be restricted (and other suspensions from that list should not).
