+There are several points to be discussed+:

* *The incentive should be structured at the fleet level*: To preserve the independence of the relationship between Bolt and the Fleet Owner, and to avoid confusion regarding any direct remuneration relationship between Bolt and the drivers, bonuses should be granted solely at the fleet level (Fleet Incentive). While these bonuses may be dependent on driver-level KPIs, the payment itself should be made exclusively to the Fleet Manager. There should be no direct entitlement for drivers, and any redistribution to them should be entirely at the discretion of the Fleet Manager. {color:#bf2600}→ could you confirm if we can proceed in this way?{color}
{color:#ffc400}Yes this is currently the case in the test. Payments are made directly to the fleet. (in fact they cannot be made to the drivers as their financial info is that of the fleet). The driver can see the amount in his app, in the same location as branded payments for example, but its up to the Fleet Owner to pass the money on to him or not, we do not intervene.{color}
* *Driver KPIs should be defined jointly with the Fleet*: Fleet-driver level engagement criteria or KPIs that condition bonuses must be negotiated and mutually agreed upon with the Fleet Owner—not unilaterally imposed by either Bolt or the Fleet. This collaborative approach ensures clarity in roles and limits the risk of control or subordination being inferred in the Bolt-driver relationship. {color:#bf2600}→ is this aligned with how this happens in practice?{color}
{color:#ffc400}Currently the thresholds are set by me, indexed to local market performance, but when getting buy-in from the Fleet Owner, I share these with him and ask if he’s OK with them. They always say yes, but there is the possibility for them to refuse. If we allowed them to negotiate things would get very complexe with cost control. {color}
* *Avoiding requalification risks through documented fleet autonomy*: To mitigate any risk of driver requalification or co-employment, it is essential that Fleet Owners retain full autonomy in defining how, whether, and under what conditions bonuses are redistributed to drivers. {color:#bf2600}→ Does the Bolt app have the technical infrastructure to allow Fleet Owners to set their own internal bonus rules (e.g., through the fleet dashboard, app interface, or written instructions), thereby reinforcing their commercial, administrative, and financial independence over their operations? Or can we do this manually for their drivers?{color}
{color:#ffc400}We do not have this kind of product complexity.{color}
• {color:#ffc400}I check driver’s ride number after a complete week and compare each driver to the thresholds. - The fleet owner has the ability to do this too within the Fleet Owner portal. {color}
• {color:#ffc400}We make payments to the {color}{color:#ffc400}*fleet*{color}{color:#ffc400} through manual compensations. The driver bonuses are paid to the Fleet, but under the driver ID (which permits the payment to show up on his app), the the Fleet bonuses under the fleet ID, but these are just forms of tagging, everything goes to the fleet. {color}
• In my discussions with the Fleet Owner, I remain open to their requests to not pay certain drivers in the case of suspected fraud for example. This has happened once. The Fleet Owner noticed a ride number was strangely high, he waited for the driver to be officially flagged and blocked by our fraud team, then requested I blacklist him from the payments. I never communicated with the driver, the Fleet Owner handled all of that. 

 

