Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd]

I believe we should be able to target previous micromobility users in Italy with communications about Bolt’s Rides launch, as both services are similar and pertain to transportation (relying on soft opt-in under ePD). In my view, this could also apply to users who have previously travelled to Italy and used Bolt there. It is reasonable to inform them that Bolt is expanding Rides into another EU country where they have used our service. As a guardrail, I would suggest limiting the targeting based on how recently they travelled and used Bolt.

We can personalise marketing using pick-up and drop-off locations, as outlined in our privacy notices under App Usage Data. However, using "live location" or history of live’ location (i.e. Bolt user visited Italy) can be problematic since we have not specified that we can use live location or its history for marketing purposes. I advise against this unless it is business-critical; then we can reassess what can be done.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
Important note - soft opt-in in Italy is permitted for emails only, but I remember that LCM/country management decided to rely on soft opt-in for all channels after benchmarking and checking that our competitors do the same in Italy.
{panel}

